Chemical models and interactive experiments — PhET, University of Colorado (@gc-phet: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_15P1XV6BQDZJM260GWM3VXHN6J
PhET Interactive Simulations, University of Colorado Boulder. [Official chemistry-simulation collection](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/filter?subjects=chemistry) · [Licensing information](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/licensing).

Use relevant simulations for balancing equations, reactants/products/leftovers, concentration, acid/base solutions, molecular shape, and polarity as they become useful. Predict the outcome before changing a control, record what the model assumes, and compare it with a calculation and a textbook explanation. A simulation illustrates a model; it is not an observation of the corresponding real chemical system.

The pages use a browser application; the automated text view did not expose the current detailed licensing notice or verify playback of each simulation. Consult the particular simulation's actual version, download availability, accessibility, and licence before retaining or reusing it. These are optional external study tools, not required Lince features or bundled software. Official collection/licensing locations checked on 29 October 2026; interactive behavior is not represented as tested.

**Return:** [General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3).
